From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kompakt: e-ink waveform and dither additions on meink

meink draws, as in 1.2; this adds to the tables and dithers it uses.

kompakt_wf_a2frames takes 8 and 9 (Caster's default A2 length): deeper
blacks and fewer traces. These only lengthen, never shortening a cold band
below its own run; 2 to 6 shorten as before.

kompakt_wf_dither 4 is blue noise: a 64x64 void-and-cluster matrix, ordered
like the Bayer patterns, so dots stay put when the picture moves, without
the grid.

The loader's dithers run on the mode's tone curve, read from meink's
EinkImage (+0x88, its 8-bit transfer at +0x300), as meink's own dither
does; without it our patterns saw lighter greys than Normal and drew text
thinner. A pixel at a sharp edge (kompakt_wf_dither_edge, 0 off) is cut to
black or white at meink's threshold of 160 instead of patterned.
kompakt_wf_dither_light (0 to 3) lifts the grey of dithered pixels towards
light so photos keep their shadows; edges keep the mode's curve.

Partial refresh: a band of changed columns is split into row runs only if
every band after it still gets one of the two boxes. A band without a box
was never refreshed but kept its old picture on the panel until something
redrew it (the app drawer showed the home screen through it). Anything left
over now goes out as a full update.

meink switches to A2 on every unblank, which left the lock screen and
everything after it on A2 whatever mode was chosen. The loader keeps the
waveform last written to waveform_mode and sets it again from an fb
notifier that runs after meink's. meink also sets A2 on every DOZE entry
and the AOD stays on it. Entering AOD over an awake screen or the sleep
picture, the loader first sets GL16 with meink's skip-clear flag down, so
meink's own GL16 to A2 switch clears black, white and redraws the newest
frame before the AOD; minute ticks re-enter DOZE over the AOD and are left
alone.

